@token = REPLACE_WITH_REAL_JWT_ONCE_AUTH_EXISTS

### Old endpoint still works
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

### New v1 endpoint - get all
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets

### New v1 endpoint - get one
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets/T001

### New v1 endpoint - filter by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets?status=OPEN

### New v1 endpoint - create a ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "VPN connection not working",
  "description": "User cannot connect to company VPN from home.",
  "category": "Network",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "createdBy": "siti@example.com"
}

### Ticket report grouped by status
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

## Ticket grouped by priority
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/reports/tickets-by-priority
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### API documentation endpoint
GET http://localhost:8080/api/docs


### NOTE: JWT auth (Day 9) is not yet implemented in this project, so there is
### no token to attach here and no 401/403 case to demonstrate. Once security
### is added, requests without a token should be rejected on both
### /api/v1/tickets/** and /api/tickets, and requests with a valid
### USER/ADMIN token should succeed:
# GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/tickets
# Authorization: Bearer <token>
